Firmware images for devices whose drivers were derived from Linux.

The free flavor is the Debian firmware-free subset and is packaged as
linux-firmware.  The nonfree flavor is packaged as linux-firmware-nonfree;
it contains the remaining linux-firmware images plus Intel CPU microcode and
depends on the free flavor.

Both flavors install plain files under ${PREFIX}/lib/firmware rather than
kernel modules.  firmware(9) searches that directory before it tries a
module of the same name, so drivers can use the Linux-firmware paths without
rebuilding the kernel.

The nonfree package also provides the raw Intel microcode files consumed by
sysutils/cpu-microcode-intel.  That port creates the early-boot blob in
/boot/firmware; the AMD equivalent is handled by
sysutils/cpu-microcode-amd.

The upstream linux-firmware project requires a licensing attestation for
firmware submitted to the collection.  Some non-free entries have vendor
EULAs, binary-only terms, or hardware-specific use restrictions; they remain
in the nonfree flavor and their WHENCE/LICENSES terms are installed with the
package.  Firmware without a redistribution grant is not included in the
upstream collection and is not packaged here.

The collection covers graphics, wireless, Bluetooth, sound, storage and
network devices.  Only images a driver actually requests are read into
kernel memory.

